# DesktopUseAgent MCP

When the user asks to control the Windows desktop, UI, apps, browser, or files via DesktopUseAgent:

1. Use MCP tools from server id **`desktopuseagent`** (Mode B: local stdio → named pipe).
2. Prefer foundation verbs first: `app_launch`, `shell_open`, `search_files`, `filesystem_*`, `clipboard_*`, `office_*`, `media_*`, adapters — one playbook per intent.
3. Discord voice: call `discord_join_voice` once — do not vision/click Discord’s server rail. Prefer `vision_ocr` over screenshot loops when reading UI text.
4. Do **not** invent screen coordinates — inspect with `desktop_get_state` / `ui_*` / `window_list` only when needed.
5. Use `input_*` / `vision_*` only as fallback when semantic/foundation paths fail.
6. Consequential actions may require Control Center approval — wait for the user. Never auto-click UAC.

No OpenAI/Anthropic API key is required for Cursor agents to use these tools.

If MCP is unavailable: tell the user to run `.\scripts\configure-cursor.ps1 -Scope user` (or install.ps1), restart Cursor, enable `desktopuseagent`, and open Control Center so the Windows Agent is running.
